What is the output of the following Java program featuring default method overriding across interface inheritance?
```java
interface AlphaNode {
    default String label() { return "Alpha"; }
}
interface BetaNode extends AlphaNode {
    default String label() { return "Beta"; }
}
class ConcreteNode implements BetaNode {}
public class NodeRunner {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        AlphaNode node = new ConcreteNode();
        System.out.println(node.label());
    }
}
```
